// The integration lane is the one place in this repo that runs in Node rather
// than in the Worker runtime: it spawns wrangler, listens on a socket, and
// hashes with node:crypto. That needs @types/node.
//
// It gets its own project rather than adding "node" to the root tsconfig's
// `types` on purpose: widening the root globally to serve one directory would
// trade a safety property for a small convenience.
//
// CORRECTED (EFB-68). This header used to claim that the root pin to
// @cloudflare/workers-types "is what stops `fs.readFileSync` from typechecking
// inside src/". That was false, and had been for a long time. The root project
// includes `tests/**`, every test imports `vitest`, and vitest's type surface
// transitively pulls @types/node — whose globals then reach every file in the
// program, `src/` included. Verified: `fs.readFileSync` and `process.env` in a
// src/ file BOTH typecheck clean under `npm run typecheck`.
//
// The pin that actually holds is `tsconfig.src.json` / `npm run typecheck:src`,
// which compiles `src/` with no tests in the program. Run THAT to know whether
// worker code has reached for a node built-in. See that file's header for the
// measurements.
//
// Checked by `npm run typecheck:integration`. It is a separate script rather
// than being chained onto `typecheck` because `typecheck` currently exits
// non-zero on 2 pre-existing errors, so an `&&` chain would never reach this
// project. Both belong in CI when CI exists.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "types": ["@cloudflare/workers-types", "node"]
  },
  // `exclude` is restated because it is inherited, and the base excludes
  // exactly this directory.
  "exclude": ["node_modules", ".wrangler"],
  "include": ["tests/integration/**/*.ts"]
}
